Construct the known component $\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\,(-5, 0)=(-5, 0). \\
\overrightarrow{AC} &=(0, 6).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](images/fa/fae0f9f3a7c91dd9aa15bedf707bd50893dc6fff510677f515a9b74250be24f8.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, 4)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Vertical scale} &=\frac{6}{4}=\frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{AC}=\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OA}+\overrightarrow{AC} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{3}{2}$.

Construct the known component $\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\,(-5, 0)=(-5, 0). \\
\overrightarrow{BC} &=(0, -7).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](images/ea/ea6e3ab1951e7aebfcce1c3ed7a26696966ba3bb0a7bb8be86e888e062e3e94e.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, -2)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Vertical scale} &=\frac{-7}{-2}=\frac{7}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{BC}=\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OB}+\overrightarrow{BC} \\
&=\mathbf{b}+\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a} \\
&=\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{a}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{7}{2}$.
